@startuml

title One verdict, reached from every writer

actor "shell, screen or job" as caller
participant "service or repository" as svc
database "the table storing the value" as db
participant "the family's trigger function" as fn
participant "ores_reporting_value_in_set_fn\n(security definer)" as verdict
database "the value set tables\n(system tenant)" as sets

caller -> svc : write a value
svc -> db : insert or update
db -> fn : before insert or update, per row
fn -> verdict : is v in set X?
verdict -> sets : read the rule
note right of verdict
  A definer function, so the read does not meet
  row level security: a tenant caller reading the
  sets itself would see none and find no rule.
end note
sets --> verdict : source_kind, bounds, pattern, values
verdict --> fn : in set, or not
fn --> db : allow, or raise naming the set and the value
db --> svc : the write, or the error
svc --> caller : the outcome

note over caller
  The engine settings proposal service asks
  ores_reporting_setting_value_verdict_fn before a
  person is asked to sign, so a proposal nobody
  could apply is refused at the desk and not at the
  trigger.
end note

@enduml
